  "text": "Allergies:\nceftriaxone\n\nChief Complaint:\nRight knee pain, Epidural abscess\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ woman with history of hypertension who had an arthrocentesis \nperformed 2 weeks ago during an outpatient orthopedic surgery \nappointment which, per report, revealed crystals c/w CPPD. She \nwas given prescriptions for meloxicam, acetaminophen/codeine, \nand cyclobenzaprine for symptomatic management. \n\nShe represented to ___ on ___ with ongoing knee \npain and fevers. She was found to have a leukocytosis to 19k and \nbe anemic with Hgb ___ ___. Repeat arthrocentesis while inpatient \nrevealed pus, but gram stain was negative. She was treated for \nseptic arthritis with vancomycin and zosyn (___) and has had \nsome improvement ___ her leukocytosis. However, she later \ndeveloped back pain and an MRI revealed an epidural collection \nat L4 as well as an 8x6cm collection ___ the iliacus muscle. She \nwas therefore transferred to ___ for neurosurgery evaluation \nand further management.\n\nInterventions:\n- ___ Arthrocentesis of R knee: reportedly c/w pseudo-gout\n- ___ Drainage of posterior R knee collection: 50cc pus \n(accidentally discarded)\n- ___ OR washout of R knee: 74k polys, many RBCs, no crystals \nor organisms\n- ___ Repeat drainage of posterior R knee collection: 15cc \ndrained\n\nOf note, ___ the process of her workup the patient had numerous \nimaging studies that demonstrated multiple bony abnormalities \nincluding a R distal femur and mid and distal tibia sclerotic \nabnormality c/f osteoblastic metastatic disease, mid and lower \nvertebral bodies with sclerotic findings.\n\nOn transfer, vitals were:  T 98.4, BP 140/96, HR 101, RR 19, Sat \n97%, Weight 78.3 kg (172 lbs)\n\nOn arrival to the MICU, the patient reported constipation (last \nbowel movement was 5 days ago) but no bowel or bladder \nincontinence or urinary retention. She endorses normal sensation \n___ her extremities, no visual changes, and no back pain.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nPRIMARY DIAGNOSES\n=================\nEpidural abscess\nIliacus abscess s/p drainage\nRight gastrocnemius abscess s/p drainage\nAbnormal skeletal imaging\nAcute kidney injury\nAnemia\nElevated trasnaminases\nCoagulopathy\nsclerotic bone lesions",
